$ jobscout nope
[stderr] unknown command "nope"

jobscout: local job-postings inventory

Usage: jobscout <command> [arguments]
       jobscout            (no command: start the dashboard; same as double-clicking it)

Commands:
  init                                                  create the database and load the starter board list
  scan                                                  fetch every board now
  search       [QUERY] [flags]                          search jobs from the terminal
  serve        [flags]                                  run the web dashboard and API (optionally with scheduled scans)
  mcp          [--allow-write]                          run the MCP server on stdio for AI agents
  board        list|add|add-url|enable|disable|rename   manage job boards
  saved        list|add|rm                              manage saved searches
  import       FILE...                                  import legacy ats-inventory-*.jsonl snapshots
  stats                                                 show datastore counts
  maintenance  [flags]                                  compress old text, prune closed jobs, vacuum
  backup       DEST.db                                  write a consistent copy of the database
  version                                               print the version

Environment: JOBSCOUT_HOME, JOBSCOUT_DB, JOBSCOUT_ADDR, JOBSCOUT_USER_AGENT, JOBSCOUT_WORKERS, JOBSCOUT_PER_HOST, JOBSCOUT_DEBUG
Run `jobscout <command> -h` for command flags.
[exit 2]

